# Stop-cage fit proof: the mechanism's FULL travel — the arch band through BOTH
# stable states plus the nub riding its apex — must clear the hard-stop cage
# everywhere; the stops bite only on over-travel or off-axis load, never during
# a normal switch. `fitcheck` renders cage ∩ travel and must be EMPTY (it is
# the check that catches a stop placed where the arch sweeps — a mechanism that
# prints fused solid). `fitcheck_neg` grows the swept zone past stop_gap so it
# MUST overlap, proving the check can fail.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
